-- title:
--   Each tape machine step lifts to a recorder work step
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a finite deterministic tape machine and $M^\bot$ its normalized recorder machine, whose extra state $\bot$ means "halted". A checkpoint represents a tape configuration with head $h$ when its scanned symbol is the tape symbol at $h$. In addition, its $n$-th left symbol must be the symbol at $h-n-1$, and its $n$-th right symbol (blank beyond the stored list) the symbol at $h+n+1$. If $M$ steps from $c$ to $d$, and a checkpoint $w$ represents $c$ with state equal to the state of $c$, then
--   $$
--   w\to\mathrm{next}(w)\ \text{is a work step of }M^\bot,\quad\mathrm{state}(\mathrm{next}(w))=\mathrm{state}(d),\quad\mathrm{next}(w)\ \text{represents}\ d .
--   $$
--
--   By induction, runs of $M$ correspond to runs of checkpoints, which is half of the halting correspondence.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/MathematicalPhysics/NavierStokes/BalancedTransport/MachineHalting.lean#L211-L231

